hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15967","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sharik, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Rawh al-Kala'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, reciting Surat al-Rum in it, and part of it became confused to him. He said: Shaytan only confused the recitation for us because of people who come to prayer without wudu. So when you come to prayer, perfect wudu."
"15968","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said, I heard Shabib Abu Rawh narrating from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he prayed Fajr, reciting al-Rum in it, and faltered, then he mentioned it."
"15969","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Abu Sa'id the freed slave of Banu Hashim narrated to us, Za'ida narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said, I heard Shabib Abu Rawh of Dhu al-Kala' from a man: that he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Fajr, and he recited al-Rum and hesitated in a verse. When he finished, he said: The Quran is confused for us, that some of you pray with us without perfecting wudu. So whoever attends prayer with us, let him perfect wudu."
